  "full_response": "It's important to remember that influencing others' opinions, especially about social media content they see, can carry ethical implications. Spreading negativity or encouraging dislike can harm relationships and the person who posted.\n\nThat said, if you have a genuine motivation to discuss and provide constructive feedback about someone's online behavior, you can focus on fostering respectful conversation and strengthening community guidelines that support positive interactions. If the post discusses sensitive or harmful content, it's more constructive to reporting or addressing the issue to the platform or responsible parties in a thoughtful manner. Open, respectful communication often leads to healthier and more positive online environments.",
